From cb42bd3874ac65e75b5f3aeb8c6150f5f8bebcbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:40:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): dial IPv6 hosts in TCP and DNS monitors

TCP and DNS monitors built their address with "%s:%d", so an IPv6 host
or resolver such as ::1 became "::1:53", which Go rejects with "too many
colons in address". Build it with net.JoinHostPort, which writes
"[::1]:53". A TCP host already written as [::1], the workaround so far,
is unwrapped first so it isn't bracketed twice.

Closes #118

Assisted-by: Claude Code
